<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Hanwha Energy 1996 net falls.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Hanwha Energy 1996 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			    231 vs     438</p>
<p>    Net				    5.7 vs    10.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     6.1 vs    11.2</p>
<p>    Turnover			 2,452.4 vs 1,909.3</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (both loss)   10.7 vs     0.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Hanwha Energy Co, one of South Korea's leading oil refiners, said a rise in crude import prices was to blame for the profit fall.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
</text>
